  "finalText": "T-1070 is re-graded and escalated, but I did not close it, so Grace's request to close it today is only partly met.\n\n- **Severity:** I raised it from sev3 to sev1. The matrix gives sev1 for payroll with company-wide impact.\n- **Escalation:** It is now escalated to incident-command, assigned to E-402 Ola Berg. She is the incident-command engineer on call when the deadline falls (shift 18:00Z–06:00Z).\n- **Deadline:** It stays at 2026-03-17T19:40Z. The sev1 response target would give an earlier time, but a committed deadline is never moved earlier.\n- **Not closed:** T-1071 is linked to T-1070 and is still open, and policy bars closing a ticket while a linked one is open. T-1071 is the payroll reporting replica lag, assigned to E-101 and due 10:30Z. E-201's comment says the batch can't be rerun until it is fixed.\n- **Handoff:** I left a comment on T-1070 for the next shift. It names T-1071 as the blocker and notes that payday is Friday. It also sets out the next steps: get T-1071 fixed, rerun the batch, confirm payments post, then close T-1070.\n\nI didn't touch T-1071 or merge the two tickets. Please tell Grace it's now sev1 and with incident command, but can't be closed until the replica lag is fixed.",
